{
 "about": "Complex creatures that work by day, take their posts at night and fight, with the platform's own fighting and every attack the one its animation was made for: a farmer who digs with a pickaxe, a knife thrower and a soldier with a sword on the player's side, a wall with a hurt box, and five foes in two groups who hit with bare hands. The models come with empty hands: the sword is a looping effect that is a model, mounted on the soldier's weapon attachment point; the pickaxe and the knife are shown by their skills while the animation holds them (scene_add_creature_skill {effect}). A stroke is a hit box triggered by the skill's graph at the moment the animation strikes; the thrown knife is a projectile that follows its target (scene_add_components {projectile:{type:\"tracking\"}}) and whose hit detection answers to enemies only and attacks with its ability unit. What to look for in the prints: SK_HP soldier / foe / wall (their full health); SK_DIG by day and none after SK_NIGHT; SK_AT shows the farmer's x going back to 3 and the thrower's and soldier's to 9.5 and 15 after SK_NIGHT; after SK_FOES: SK_TARGET soldier on / thrower on, SK_THROW then SK_KNIFE_HIT and SK_HURT, SK_SLASH then SK_HIT soldier 40, SK_PUNCH then SK_HIT foe 25, SK_DOWN foe; a foe that gets as far as the wall: SK_AT_WALL, SK_WALL n going down; after SK_DAY the foes that are left run back. Every run goes differently, the cooldowns are random: in the run written up in WALKTHROUGH.md (2026-10-11, the fourth) the soldier cut down all five and the wall was never reached; in the one before, the second group brought the soldier down (SK_DOWN soldier), two of them hammered the wall from 200 to 100 and fell to the thrower's knives. The knife's ability unit asks for 0 x attack + 40 and takes 18 (SK_HURT): what an ability unit deals is reduced, what a hit box deals is not. The screenshots and the recording show the pickaxe, the knife in the hand and in the air, the sword and the health bars.",
